# Throwaway harnesses review lenses write while checking a fix. They have Bash
# access on purpose — one examined 432,954 graph swaps to verify an objective — but
# nothing tells an agent to clean up, and a probe left under app/test or lib/test
# gets picked up by vitest, runs for 90 s, times out, and reads as a FAILING test
# on the next run. Give them somewhere that is neither a test glob nor tracked.
# `scripts/hygiene/run.mjs` still fails on an untracked file under */test/, so this
# is a designated place to work, not a way to hide residue.
.review-scratch/

# tsc --build cache; regenerated on demand and machine-specific.
*.tsbuildinfo
